🚩 Saturated topics — these prompts get flagged
We have enough of the topics below. A prompt written on one will be flagged even if it is otherwise well built. Reach for the ✅ list instead.

Extrapolation
🚩 Frame exit · collision along a path · direction of travel
✅ Acceleration/deceleration ("will she stop before the curb?") · trend over time (queue growing, water rising) · interception ("will these two meet, and where?") · occlusion mid-path ("in front of or behind the pillar?") · reactive agents ("would the cyclist swerve, and which way?") · "cannot be determined" answers

Hidden & Invisible
🚩 Light / sun / shadow · wind
✅ Wetness · dust · heat · sound sources · force & tension · reflections · blur · container contents from deformation or handling · material properties (heavy, hot, fragile) · what is behind the camera

Affordance & Feasibility
🚩 Vehicles · falling straight down · insertion and fit · motion
✅ Stability & tipping · load-bearing · support & stacking · grasp span · tool adequacy ("is the ladder tall enough?") · sequencing ("couch out without moving the table?") · deformability (roll, fold, squeeze, bend) · aperture mismatch (fits by area, not cross-section) · timing ("cross before the train arrives?") · collaboration (can A and B do it together?) · who or which can do it · 3D volume · arc & radius · liquid volume · aggregate packing (all the books re-shelved)

Spatial "Alien Viewpoint" & Reachability
🚩 Binary can-you-see · graded occlusion (full/partial/none) · "if you turned left, could you see"
✅ Reachability ("reach the top shelf without standing?") · two-agent joint reach ("pass the box without moving their feet?") · mutual visibility (both ways or one?) · facing as a viewpoint proxy · non-human viewpoints · very large or very small scenes · how many / when / how / where / why · "nothing blocks it" answers

Theory of Mind
🚩 Intention · emotion
✅ Belief, knowledge, attitude, attention · false belief & knowledge asymmetry ("A hides it while B is away — where will B look?") · perspective divergence · deception & concealment · second order ("does she realise he knows?") · surprise as a violated expectation · sarcasm · embarrassment, pride, shame · predicting action from a mistaken belief · genuinely ambiguous mental states

Change & Consequence
🚩 Fall or detachment · impact target (what it hits)
✅ Liquid & spill ("where does it flow, what gets wet?") · thermal & state change · removal — what fills or is exposed · load transfer ("if he lets go, who bears the weight?") · consequence on a process rather than an object · longer horizon (falls, then rolls, then what) · reversibility · rotational, optical and fluid effects · "in order to do X, what should a person do?" · "nothing happens, and here's why" answers

